{
  "about": "Counts per official rulebook: entries in the book, entries DAS · Core covers (`core`), entries das-rulepack covers (`rulepack`). Counts only: no names of entries, no text.",
  "method": "Static comparison by name. Each entry of a book's catalogue (spells, feats, optional features, items, class and subclass features, monsters) is counted once, under the book the catalogue files it in; its name, turned into a dnd5e-style identifier, is looked up among the identifiers of DAS · Core, then among those of das-rulepack (an entry found in both is counted under `core`). A dedicated entry is not proof that the rule works, and no entry does not mean it does not: much is resolved from the item's own data.",
  "computed": "2026-11-19",
  "copied": "2026-11-20",
  "source": "books.coverage.json of the DAS workspace audit (not part of this repository)",
  "note": "`computed` is the date of the audit file. `rulepack` is the audit's count on that date. tools/books-progress.mjs recomputes it from scripts/rules/books/ and uses its own figure. `foundry` is the id of the official Foundry VTT package of the book, from docs/foundry-modules.json, or null. The `monster` kind is measured differently: see `monsters`.",
  "monsters": {
    "method": "A monster has no dedicated entry: DAS · Core plays its features one by one. Every feature of the stat block (traits, actions, bonus actions, reactions, legendary and mythic actions, spellcasting) gets one verdict: an entry of DAS · Core under the feature's identifier; a rule the engine reads from the text (computed with the engine's own pure function); resolved by the item's data (an attack, a save, spellcasting); no combat mechanic in the text; or open. A monster is resolved when none of its features is open. In the `monster` kind: `total` = monsters, `core` = monsters resolved, `pack` = 0, `features` = their features, `featuresResolved` = features that are not open.",
    "limits": "Static reading of the dataset's text, not of the Foundry data, and not proof of play. \"Resolved by data\" does not check what follows an attack (its riders); \"no combat mechanic\" is a heuristic on the words of the text; a variant copied from another creature inherits its features without the changes applied.",
    "computed": "2026-11-20",
    "copied": "2026-11-20",
    "source": "monsters.features.json of the DAS workspace audit (not part of this repository)"
  },
